  "refuter_findings": [
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:3:1",
      "id": "ex-gauges-of-norm-balls-and-ellipsoids",
      "location": "Example",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The Example states: \"Both are norms because their sets are absorbing, balanced, and have zero intersection with every nontrivial line only at $0$.\" This asserted set property is false. For any nonzero v, the line L=span(v) meets B(0,r) in nonzero points, for example rv/(2||v||). Likewise, if q is positive definite, tv is a nonzero point of E for every sufficiently small t>0. The displayed gauge formulas do yield norms, but not for the stated reason.",
